## Why This Is Asked
This question tests understanding of runtime configurability, deduplication logic, and offset management—skills essential for building robust streaming pipelines in production systems.

## Key Concepts
- **Runtime config updates**: Using a dedicated configuration topic to dynamically control sink behavior
- **Per-message deduplication**: Maintaining deduplication state across message processing
- **Toggle behavior**: Safely switching deduplication on/off without losing in-flight messages
- **At-least-once semantics**: Ensuring offsets commit even when deduplication is bypassed
- **Graceful state management**: Handling the transition between dedup-enabled and disabled modes

## Code Example
```javascript
class RuntimeConfig {
  constructor() { this.disableDedup = false; }

  apply(event) {
    if (typeof event.disableDedup === 'boolean') {
      this.disableDedup = event.disableDedup;
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test race conditions between config updates and incoming messages?
- What happens to deduplication state when the connector restarts?
- How would you implement this using Kafka Streams instead of a sink connector?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to implement dynamic, production-friendly routing logic that doesn't require restart, a common real-world pattern.

## Key Concepts

- Thread-safe configuration reloads
- Atomic map swap and minimal in-flight coordination
- Per-message offset handling for at-least-once semantics
- Lightweight canary tests for config reload

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal skeleton illustrating API surfaces
class Router {
  constructor() { this.routing = new Map([['events_A','sink1'], ['events_B','sink2']]); this.lock = false; }
  onConfigReload(newMap) { /* atomically swap */ }
  processMessage(topic, msg) { const sink = this.routing.get(topic); this.emit(sink, msg); }
  emit(sink, msg) { /* write to sink and commit offset */ }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test config reload under high-throughput? 
- How handle partial reloads if the new routing map is invalid?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests stateful cross-topic streaming, per-key windowing, offset management, and recovery semantics within KCNA.

## Key Concepts
- Stateful cross-topic join for userId
- Per-topic offset preservation and replay safety
- 15-second tumbling window with watermark handling
- State snapshotting to a compacted 'kcna_state' topic
- Exactly-once vs at-least-once emission guarantees and dedup

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: join processor sketch
class JoinProcessor {
  constructor() {
    this.profileCache = new Map();
    this.window = new TumblingWindow(15); // in seconds
  }
  onClick(click) {
    const pid = this.profileCache.get(click.userId);
    if (pid) emitEnriched({ ...click, profileVersion: pid.version });
    // else stash or wait for profile
  }
  onProfile(profile) {
    this.profileCache.set(profile.userId, profile);
  }
  onWindowEmit(windowId) {
    // snapshot state to kcna_state and commit
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
